	"_shade_bake_note": "M2W1 astraA (F5, OQ-ART-WORLD): a shade baked at load into the glb structure meshes (WorldKitMeshes.bake_shade; the glb is unchanged): UV2.y = 0.5 + (m - 1) / (2 shade_range), CUSTOM0.y = shade_range, CUSTOM0.z = grime (the share of the shader's world-height grime the structure keeps). m = part x paint_value[paint] x contact x facing x by_type.gain. part = the glb's own per-part shade at part_shade (the shader's), so with enabled false nothing changes (the glb's UV2, no CUSTOM0.y, the shader's old path). contact: faces that do not look up darken towards the piece's ground (its origin) over height_m, to ground at y 0; a vertex of a face taller than span_ref_m gets span_ref_m / span of it (a face interpolates between its corners). up / down: faces with normal y >= / <= normal_y get gain. skip_paints keep their part shade only. by_type: the summit pieces one step brighter (F2), gate fronts a little brighter than walls. Cover looks use the shade_range and part_shade too (their parts' \"shade\").",
	"shade_bake": {
		"enabled": true,
		"shade_range": 0.6,
		"part_shade": 0.08,
		"grime": 0.5,
		"paint_value": {"rock": 0.52, "dark": 0.78, "plate_dark": 0.78, "travertine_shade": 0.64, "travertine": 0.72, "marble": 0.88, "timber": 0.82, "leather": 0.86, "bronze": 0.8, "gold": 0.95, "canvas": 0.92, "legion_red": 0.95, "roof_tile": 0.92},
		"_glb_note": "M2W1 r2a (OQ-ART-WORLD, placeholders): the geometry part of the shade, baked by tools/blender/m2w1_world_kit.py into the glb's UV2.y as 0.5 + (m - 1) / (2 shade_range) (skip_paints keep their raw part shade): m = part shade (at part_shade; builders write threshold and tread wear there) x contact x occlusion. contact.<family>: faces that do not look up darken towards the piece's ground (y 0) to ground over height_m, the band's top wobbling by up to uneven_m; such faces are split at split_m. ao.<family>: rays cosine-weighted rays of ray_m against the look's own triangles per vertex position and face normal; m *= 1 - strength x min(occlusion, max) x min(1, face_ref_m / the face's longest edge). The load-time bake (WorldKitMeshes.bake_shade) multiplies paint_value, up / down and by_type gain on top; one place per term. enabled false: the glb's UV2 as is, the shader's old path.",
